  "description": "<div>\n<p>Arrange <code>n</code> queens on an <code>n</code>-by-<code>n</code> board so that no two share a row, column, or diagonal. Represent a board as an array of row strings: <code>Q</code> marks a queen, and <code>.</code> marks an unused square.</p>\n<p>Return all valid boards. The rows within each board must be in top-to-bottom order; sort the list of boards lexicographically by their row-string arrays (ordinary string order, where <code>.</code> precedes <code>Q</code>). Return <code>[]</code> if no arrangement exists.</p>\n<p><strong>Example 1:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 1\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[&quot;Q&quot;]]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> The sole square holds the single queen.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 2:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 2\n<strong>Output:</strong> []\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> Every two-queen arrangement has a shared column or diagonal.</pre>\n<p><strong>Example 3:</strong></p>\n<pre><strong>Input:</strong> n = 4\n<strong>Output:</strong> [[&quot;..Q.&quot;,&quot;Q...&quot;,&quot;...Q&quot;,&quot;.Q..&quot;],[&quot;.Q..&quot;,&quot;...Q&quot;,&quot;Q...&quot;,&quot;..Q.&quot;]]\n<strong>Explanation:</strong> These are the two valid four-queen boards, ordered by their first rows.</pre>\n<p><strong>Constraints:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><code>1 &lt;= n &lt;= 8</code></li>\n</ul>\n</div>",
